	year = {2016},
	booktitle = {{Proceedings of the European Conference on Games-based Learning}},
	volume = {2016-January},
	pages = {98-107},
	abstract = {The highly theoretical methodology, in which software engineering is frequently taught, causes that learners usually lose their interest in learning software engineering. This study introduce SmartProject, a learning environment based on serious games and social networks to teach and motivate learners in software engineering, and evaluates its educational effectiveness. Computer Science undergraduate students at the University of Cadiz in Spain participated in a pilot study based on case of study to assess the educational effectiveness of SmartProject, in terms of motivation, user experience and learning outcomes. The results of the pilot study give a preliminary feedback about the educational effectiveness of SmartProject as a learning environment, and show that participants enjoyed with the experience and felt well motivate using it. Moreover, the participants' opinions allow us to conclude that participants think that learning approaches such as using serious games, gamification and social networks are useful and effective to help and motivate learners in their knowledge acquisition. © The Authors, 2016. All Rights Reserved.},
	author_keywords = {Gamification; Serious games; Social networks; Software engineering},
	keywords = {Computer aided instruction; Engineering education; Learning systems; Social networking (online); Social sciences computing; Software engineering; Students; Educational effectiveness; Gamification; Learning approach; Learning environments; Learning outcome; Pilot studies; Undergraduate students; User experience; Serious games},
